# VS Code REST Client examples. Use an APIM subscription ID configuration and a valid
# subscription key supplied only in your personal, untracked REST Client environment.
# Model and operation names must match the configured APIM API and price cards.
@gateway = https://your-gateway.azure-api.net

### Non-streaming: APIM reserves, backend executes, actual usage settles
POST {{gateway}}/foundry/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain why budget caps differ from TPM limits."}],
  "max_tokens": 64,
  "stream": false
}

### Streaming: conservative reservation, no client-supplied cache discount
POST {{gateway}}/foundry/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Describe cached input token pricing."}],
  "max_tokens": 64,
  "stream": true
}

### Language sentiment: record count rounds per document
POST {{gateway}}/language/sentiment
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "documents": [
    {"id": "1", "language": "en", "text": "The example is easy to understand."},
    {"id": "2", "language": "en", "text": "The rate-limit decision is visible."}
  ]
}

### Document Intelligence: selected pages are enforced on the backend, not just claimed
POST {{gateway}}/document-intelligence/analyze?pages=1-2
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "base64Source": "{{$processEnv SAMPLE_PDF_BASE64}}"
}

# Follow the returned gateway Operation-Location with the same identity.
# Do not call a raw backend URL or reuse another principal's operation ID.
